.* QHRSCMD: command help. Generated by `cargo run -p helpaudit -- gen` from the
.* definitions and command/sys-cpps/help/; do not edit.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=RST.Restore Object (RST)
:P.Use the Restore Object (RST) command to restore IFS objects.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RST/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RST/OBJ'.Objects (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Include or omit
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.Included.
:PT.:PK.*OMIT:EPK.
:PD.Left out.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. New object name
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RST/PATTERN'.Name pattern (PATTERN)
:P.The name pattern for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Pattern
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Include or omit
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.Included.
:PT.:PK.*OMIT:EPK.
:PD.Left out.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RST/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:PT.:PK.*DIR:EPK.
:PD.The directory and the objects in it, but not its subdirectories'
contents.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*OBJ:EPK.
:PD.The object only.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RST/SYSTEM'.Restore to system (SYSTEM)
:P.The restore to system for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LCL:EPK.
:PD.Local.
:PT.:PK.*RMT:EPK.
:PD.Remote.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RST/OPTION'.Option (OPTION)
:P.The option for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PK.*OLD:EPK.
:PD.The old one.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RST/ALWOBJDIF'.Allow object differences (ALWOBJDIF)
:P.Which differences between the saved object and the object on the
system are allowed when it is restored.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:PT.:PK.*PGP:EPK.
:PD.The primary group.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AUTL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RST/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:P.Up to 75 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RST/LABEL'.Label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SEARCH:EPK.
:PD.The value is searched for.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RST/OPTFILE'.Optical file (OPTFILE)
:P.The path of the file on the optical volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RST/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SEARCH:EPK.
:PD.The value is searched for.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RST/ENDOPT'.End of media option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RST/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
